  "aiContextParagraph": "Vice President Gibran Rakabuming Raka has formally resigned from his office, officially notifying the People's Consultative Assembly of his decision. Following the announcement, reports confirm that he has departed from the Vice Presidential Palace. President Prabowo Subianto acknowledged the resignation with reservations, noting the difficulty of the situation. Public and political reactions remain divided regarding the motivation behind this move. Members of the Golkar faction in the People's Consultative Assembly characterized the resignation as an act of statesmanship. Conversely, representatives from the PDIP North Sumatra branch suggested the action may have been a strategy intended to circumvent potential impeachment proceedings. The resignation process occurred over three days of heightened political activity and has had immediate economic implications, with the national currency dropping to a record-low value against international benchmarks as observers monitor the resulting governmental instability.",
